# Runtime secrets for the containers. This template is committed; the
# real file is NOT and must never be.
#
# Lives ON THE SERVER at <DEPLOY_PATH>/.env.production. Create it there
# once, by hand — deploy.sh refuses to deploy without it, on purpose:
# the alternative is a site that looks fine and silently drops every
# waitlist signup.
#
#     ssh <user>@<host>
#     cd /srv/ergoflo-landing
#     cp .env.production.example .env.production
#     nano .env.production
#     chmod 600 .env.production
#
# `git reset --hard` during deploy does not touch untracked files, so
# this survives every deploy.

# --- Supabase (read by lib/supabase.ts, server-side only) ------------
# Settings → API in the Supabase dashboard.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY is the service-role key: it bypasses row-level
# security. It is server-only and must never be given a NEXT_PUBLIC_
# prefix — that would ship it to every visitor's browser.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# --- Caddy / Let's Encrypt (read by the Caddyfile) -------------------
# Where Let's Encrypt sends certificate-expiry warnings if automatic
# renewal ever stops working. Use an inbox someone actually reads —
# this is the only warning you get before the site goes untrusted.
ACME_EMAIL=
